# Olfactory bulb project context

When working on code related to the olfactory bulb (OB) model, TMR report, homeostatic plasticity, or the notebooks in this repo:

1. **Use `.cursor/PROJECT_CONTEXT.md` as the source of truth** for:
   - Mathematical model (Naka–Rushton, OB equations, fixed-point structure)
   - Notation (b, g, r, y, gr, θ, α, W, σ, Hessian, PPR)
   - Parameter fitting (loss, targets 0.5, Adam, constraints)
   - Stability analysis (Jacobian, eigenvalues of A)
   - Output-preserving Δθ and Hessian eigen-directions

If the user has not attached `PROJECT_CONTEXT.md`, refer to it or summarise from it when answering questions about the model, equations, or project goals.
